# Firebase Configuration Setup Guide

## Current Issue
The Firebase project `tempcomm-35dff` is returning "CONFIGURATION_NOT_FOUND" error, which means:
1. The project doesn't exist or isn't accessible
2. Firebase Authentication isn't enabled
3. The API configuration is incorrect

## Solution Options

### Option 1: Provide Your Firebase Configuration
When you provide your Firebase token/configuration, I'll update the Angular environment with your Firebase project details:

```typescript
export const environment = {
  production: false,
  firebase: {
    apiKey: "YOUR_API_KEY",
    authDomain: "YOUR_PROJECT.firebaseapp.com",
    databaseURL: "https://YOUR_PROJECT-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com",
    projectId: "YOUR_PROJECT_ID",
    storageBucket: "YOUR_PROJECT.appspot.com",
    messagingSenderId: "YOUR_SENDER_ID",
    appId: "YOUR_APP_ID"
  }
};
```

### Option 2: Use Firebase Emulator (For Testing)
I can set up Firebase emulators for local development:

```typescript
export const environment = {
  production: false,
  firebase: {
    apiKey: "fake-api-key",
    authDomain: "localhost",
    databaseURL: "http://localhost:9000?ns=YOUR_PROJECT_ID",
    projectId: "YOUR_PROJECT_ID",
    storageBucket: "localhost",
    messagingSenderId: "0",
    appId: "1:0:web:fake-app-id"
  }
};
```

